Description:

Analyzed a multi-country dataset of over 50,000 time-series records in Python to evaluate the relationship between government stringency measures, socioeconomic indicators (HDI, GDP per capita), and COVID-19 spread metrics (total cases and deaths).

Extracted and audited the raw data using Pandas, performing a comprehensive missing-value analysis that identified and isolated 6,202 unrecorded entries in the Human Development Index column while verifying completeness across epidemiological variables. 

Visualized feature distributions and statistical variances using Matplotlib and Seaborn across 6 core metrics, establishing a clean data pipeline for downstream modeling and correlation analysis.
